# editors use the modern React hooks pattern from reactor-browser

Document editors follow a consistent pattern using auto-generated hooks from `@powerhousedao/reactor-browser`:

```typescript
import { generateId } from "document-model/core";
import { useSelectedTodoDocument } from "todo-app/document-models/todo";
import { addTodo } from "todo-app/document-models/todo";

export default function Editor() {
  const [document, dispatch] = useSelectedTodoDocument();

  function handleAddTodo(values: { title: string }) {
    if (values.title) {
      dispatch(addTodo({ id: generateId(), title: values.title }));
    }
  }
}
```

Key points:
- `useSelectedXDocument` is auto-generated per document model — since [[useSelectedDocument hook is auto-generated per document model]], never implement it manually
- The hook **and** the action creators both come from the same document-model barrel (`todo-app/document-models/todo`) — not from a deep `gen/creators.js` path, and not from an `editors/hooks/` folder
- Since `generateId()` from `document-model` is non-deterministic (it returns `globalThis.crypto.randomUUID()`), IDs must be generated in the editor **before** dispatch and passed through the action input -- never inside the reducer, which must stay replay-deterministic

